{"title":"2001 AIME II Problems/Problem 14","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/3/f93f5c51ea4b04b4992b003b39479f29018f6bda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2n$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Complex_number\" title=\"Complex number\">complex numbers</a> that satisfy both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/9/fb9242a937b24c8b163d839d6f21571c3245a399.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^{28} - z^{8} - 1 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"126\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/0/c40472d6494c815b03e15cd33aa72003b4b9615a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mid z \\mid = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" />. These numbers have the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/7/037f71707e471abdc8cd57ffad13be386ff6ade4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_{m} = \\cos\\theta_{m} + i\\sin\\theta_{m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"170\" height=\"15\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/9/6b9834b8ca5a1fd3bf39528191f6191aeee7eee6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\leq\\theta_{1} &lt; \\theta_{2} &lt; \\ldots &lt; \\theta_{2n} &lt; 360$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"234\" height=\"15\" /> and angles are measured in degrees. Find the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/1/d71cedb41c9028bce7b55df16e5557501e17977a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta_{2} + \\theta_{4} + \\ldots + \\theta_{2n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"143\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Solution_2_more_in_depth)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Solution 2 more in depth)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Solution_2_more_in_depth.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Solution_2_more_in_depth)\">Solution 1 (Solution 2 more in depth)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Solution 2 more in depth)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/1/83147269611ed30c50eb2ddeb1b275003b3ab032.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|z| = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"18\" />, then it is evident that both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/6/406c350f7c6e85958c708328053adb390ddba158.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|z^{28}| = |z^8| = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"120\" height=\"21\" />. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/c/1ecb323cab851eed132ccdb652492c456c8a4b14.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^{28} - z^8 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"97\" height=\"18\" />. Say <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/f/75f8d05eee0cae840a823e533cfa6f53eae52dac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^{28} = a+bi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/3/df3aa5d47f3cda332816762f8ed873153ac84363.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^8 = r+si$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"88\" height=\"18\" />. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/1/881a13b9434a980760aa82048f3589b3480a04d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a-r + (b-s)i = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"157\" height=\"20\" />, in which through equivalation of real and imaginary parts, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/f/a4f7389531d609c141ba2902d92d74b27d7d62f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=r+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/9/4e9e79a2f4c6901ebd3baab99e9ab0b7611a7685.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=s$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" />, in which we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/3/9b3eb1c644eb3d366b87855fbd28baa70cabdba8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^{28} = (1+r)+si$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"141\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/3/df3aa5d47f3cda332816762f8ed873153ac84363.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^8 = r+si$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"88\" height=\"18\" />. Then, because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/a/37a64df4223f5c7e0d510302a11841ccff369213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|z^{28}|=|z^8|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"86\" height=\"21\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/c/69c73b69da0c46373b3046e0e462a5754a3b5a12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1+r)^2+s^2 = r^2+s^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"180\" height=\"21\" />, in which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/2/e92871b17efeb97e609638904df434f0de631c60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=-\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"62\" height=\"38\" />. Then, substituting into the definition of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/a/e3a40f7fe971577db71f8a813c51fe18058f0d7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|z^8|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"29\" height=\"21\" />, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/4/394811da7a236fdc8f04b0fe3133f19401087ffb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s=\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"77\" height=\"43\" />. Thus, we have two cases.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/f/d7fc8bd87f70c04687e145d72c7b03b4d902f80d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{Case 1:}$\" width=\"59\" height=\"11\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/6/ad6317628b9f650b40298aa0e3daa2f428f86112.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^{28}=\\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}i, z^8=\\frac{-1}{2}+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"252\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>In this case, we rewrite everything in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/2/6026d0234606add2949768dac34641de4a1dfbb7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{cis}(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"45\" height=\"20\" />. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/f/92feefb97e24e50227777a399896cb7e34cb40fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^{28} = \\text{cis}(\\frac{\\pi}{3})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"97\" height=\"34\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/2/f92b98bbc5b290c880b5ac64583aca8a0c4bba96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^8=\\text{cis}(\\frac{2\\pi}{3})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"100\" height=\"38\" />. Then, because each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/5/4c5fcaaf709b30b98b697c48f5384427b0c0f79c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_m = \\text{cis}(\\theta_m)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"101\" height=\"20\" />, we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/c/b9c29f2300fe3bc08cf3a77f067c2add2b3eef7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{cis}(28\\theta)=\\text{cis}(\\frac{\\pi}{3})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"134\" height=\"34\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/2/9a2d90471c44ee17a93fe431650564ccee889993.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{cis}(8\\theta)=\\text{cis}(\\frac{2\\pi}{3})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"134\" height=\"38\" />. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a42bb181459c4dbe2f646049fb940ec7c6a8e28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$28\\theta \\equiv \\frac{\\pi}{3} \\mod 2\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"141\" height=\"34\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/8/2281a3ff710768661574ac4ce08861652474d079.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8\\theta \\equiv \\frac{2\\pi}{3} \\mod 2\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"141\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>The second congruence gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/1/281f36c329f385e776303800c9cd0da9bf1f63bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta \\equiv \\frac{\\pi}{12} \\mod \\frac{\\pi}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"125\" height=\"34\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/b/16b7676f95e59f76d3a380bd936f8900c8b25fab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta = \\frac{\\pi}{12} + \\frac{\\pi}{4}k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"105\" height=\"34\" />. Substitution into the first modulo gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/d/50dcb00f0b439cf1c0335bbb39addc297612f8dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{7\\pi}{3} + 7\\pi k \\equiv \\frac{\\pi}{3} \\mod 2\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"191\" height=\"38\" />, in which subtracting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/2/2d2d0dc818ffa40c824ec87c9ad9c51fa86f458d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\pi}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"13\" height=\"33\" /> gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/5/4f53e52e8c1e8296b84fb97068fc03702f57f4cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\pi+7\\pi k\\equiv 0 \\mod 2\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"181\" height=\"16\" />. This only holds if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/b/ceb89ec2cbdeebb1d7ad70c4b39301933f697cb9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=2m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"14\" />, and thus we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/5/915da12e35483a3d48641120466c4cf30e7106ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta = \\frac{\\pi}{12} + \\frac{\\pi m}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"110\" height=\"34\" />. The solutions in incremental order to this case are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/1/3413c7476e4ba6a7c65f516777c5e806aee1cfd0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\pi}{12},\\; \\frac{7\\pi}{12},\\; \\frac{13\\pi}{12},\\; \\frac{19\\pi}{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"154\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/1/331226e700ae378565242419f911b29b000845c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{Case 2:}$\" width=\"59\" height=\"11\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/f/d6fb49b45f8910537010bc3bcf042cd76b4cf90f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^{28}=\\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}i, z^8=\\frac{-1}{2}-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"252\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Once again, conversion into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/2/6026d0234606add2949768dac34641de4a1dfbb7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{cis}(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"45\" height=\"20\" /> form and using De Moivre's gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/e/64e521769487f1386501d2edf5e2146a9cb752e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$28\\theta \\equiv -\\frac{\\pi}{3} \\mod 2\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"156\" height=\"34\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/e/60e4c3147cd0263c80470deb1c306cbbe36f9285.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8\\theta \\equiv -\\frac{2\\pi}{3} \\mod 2\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"156\" height=\"38\" />. Once again, the second equation gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/1/0e1aab7ba538f67bcbe2c0a723f6825c10307118.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta = -\\frac{\\pi}{12} + \\frac{\\pi}{4}k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"119\" height=\"34\" />. Substitution of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> into the first again gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/6/6c6299a8c6e57129914e9da9603dbf3ab4475c60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$28x=28(-\\frac{\\pi}{12} + \\frac{\\pi k}{4})=-\\frac{7\\pi}{3}+7\\pi k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"285\" height=\"39\" />, in which reducing modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/9/709acef3551b886e6754de72d59a88f00660f0d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"14\" /> and adding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/2/2d2d0dc818ffa40c824ec87c9ad9c51fa86f458d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\pi}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"13\" height=\"33\" />, we obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/f/daf61d4787932393928176a70f8b2cbc7110e9ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\frac{2\\pi}{3}+7\\pi k \\equiv 0 \\pmod{2\\pi}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"209\" height=\"38\" />. Once again, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/b/ceb89ec2cbdeebb1d7ad70c4b39301933f697cb9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=2m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"14\" />, and so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/7/5c7cb86ea4f995e3e063cf183417e76f16a21b18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta = -\\frac{\\pi}{12} + \\frac{\\pi m}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"125\" height=\"34\" />. The solutions for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/5/0e57249e7169e1b5c1e8c6c7758818e85723b422.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5\\pi}{12},\\;\\frac{11\\pi}{12},\\; \\frac{17\\pi}{12},\\; \\frac{23\\pi}{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"165\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>Converting everything into degrees and putting in incremental order, we see that each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/3/2b393bbcfb393061428cec7fcfc6b653e978252a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta_m : 1\\le m\\le 8 = 15^\\circ,\\;75^\\circ,\\;105^\\circ,\\;165^\\circ,\\;195^\\circ,\\;255^\\circ,\\;285^\\circ,\\;345^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"498\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Adding each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/9/0f91f49881f3adf02c52dbc763da878659a3bd8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta_{2k} : 1 \\le k \\le 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"117\" height=\"17\" />, we obtain a final answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/8/798a2bcac5193d032f6135b9e85524d472069ab4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$75+165+255+345 = \\boxed{840}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"231\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> can be written in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/8/3789d5ad6c8db328dcbeed3d5c25ceea54c13177.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{cis\\,}\\theta$\" width=\"30\" height=\"13\" />. Rearranging, we find that  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/4/1348521623b85f286657255b8b1ea90b7a882990.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{cis\\,}{28}\\theta = \\text{cis\\,}{8}\\theta+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"142\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Since the real part of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/3/683b7174efe9c507f920aced85edc8699f00e5d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{cis\\,}{28}\\theta$\" width=\"48\" height=\"13\" /> is one more than the real part of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/6/976ad819aa3d760090027d3c43061fa77b505cee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{cis\\,} {8}\\theta$\" width=\"39\" height=\"13\" /> and their imaginary parts are equal, it is clear that either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/b/debab7f1b67f93945bce1360931855043f12fe73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{cis\\,}{28}\\theta = \\frac{1}{2}+\\frac {\\sqrt{3}}{2}i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"142\" height=\"41\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/2/cb27726f20fc6ebec9bd4edae20870210a4987fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{cis\\,} {8}\\theta =  -\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac {\\sqrt{3}}{2}i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"147\" height=\"41\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/b/3fbd16484a2cb82ec6e8f080f61992ada5467130.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{cis\\,}{28}\\theta = \\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"142\" height=\"41\" /> and  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/9/529c0da1b098538dbd37f6e2e128d89e3bbb3fef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{cis\\,} {8}\\theta =  -\\frac{1}{2}- \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"147\" height=\"41\" />\n</p>\n<ul><li>Case 1 &#160;: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/0/0d03e13c6407075f5bcda9f720d92b70c279b9cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{cis\\,}{28}\\theta = \\frac{1}{2}+ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"142\" height=\"41\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/b/47b4bf6f4494b98f3b16e3ca52364b544db4f789.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{cis\\,} {8}\\theta =  -\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"147\" height=\"41\" /></li></ul>\n<p>Setting up and solving equations, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/0/a40c5f59ce699abafeb2157cd5e54cbea54f9ddf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z^{28}= \\text{cis\\,}{60^\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"101\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/0/92044ccabbda3532f24fb713189c7c8b9a01dc28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z^8= \\text{cis\\,}{120^\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"99\" height=\"15\" />, we see that the solutions common to both equations have arguments <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/4/2a44f01b84b23bec8d925e4058cc08435c39c79e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15^\\circ , 105^\\circ, 195^\\circ,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"116\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/9/0b95d695423963179c038fb1e78a98f068dff917.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ 285^\\circ$\" width=\"38\" height=\"13\" />. We can figure this out by adding 360 repeatedly to the number 60 to try and see if it will satisfy what we need. We realize that it does not work in the integer values.\n</p>\n<ul><li>Case 2 &#160;: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/2/292d5774d2f206bbbe6a317934cd4d6168422a68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{cis\\,}{28}\\theta = \\frac{1}{2} -\\frac {\\sqrt{3}}{2}i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"142\" height=\"41\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/986989213eeea0a79b887cce1e06357f3271b6ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{cis\\,} {8}\\theta =  -\\frac {1}{2} -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"147\" height=\"41\" /></li></ul>\n<p>Again setting up equations (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/1/d91c0acc2449ecc98585eaffd544f3d2be53828c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z^{28}= \\text{cis\\,}{300^\\circ}$\" width=\"106\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/5/f151e65a8c8e4e50342b0d9c60efcb809198031c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z^{8} = \\text{cis\\,}{240^\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"99\" height=\"15\" />) we see that the common solutions have arguments of  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/6/4a68fa0f30f8339e1c78db71c0459646d70be9a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$75^\\circ, 165^\\circ, 255^\\circ,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"116\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/0/3103dddcb3027022c591426086d455300a2b0f4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$345^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"33\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>Listing all of these values, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/1/d71cedb41c9028bce7b55df16e5557501e17977a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta_{2} + \\theta_{4} + \\ldots + \\theta_{2n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"143\" height=\"15\" /> is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/a/2caf6fa9176b3f05b3c7f25905f601ef6e062aa4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(75 + 165 + 255 + 345) ^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"186\" height=\"18\" /> which is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/3/da317bda5d04c568660361b5cbb013205ff6bfd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {840}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" /> degrees. We only want the sum of a certain number of theta, not all of it.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/2/4b2f8e91b1d116e909176d1d77b58dbf2bfbf4f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|z^8|=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"62\" height=\"21\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/f/01f7aac3e57f997317789dcd4368f8a7b07ebc24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|z|=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"18\" />. Therefore we write <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/8/2281da306af0c37d9ab7c4145bf7e0432c18ef8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|z^{28} -1|=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"100\" height=\"21\" />. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/7/bb73338ac58783a3434586078368975073c24144.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(z^{28} -1)(z^{-28} -1)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"183\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>We now express <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/b/6fb300dacfcde1b57ad070409262b1743e0cd966.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"24\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/5/bb5e108fdc4bf4fb6151cb922992f23bc6c35985.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos$\" width=\"24\" height=\"8\" />, \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/9/e0962b07ed70790ea97b5c031f9f1be5d2f7160d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^28=\\cos(28\\theta) + i\\sin(28\\theta)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"213\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/1/1e1d6fb911f9f9938abf8928b69f4e3f580df0f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^{-28}=\\cos(28\\theta) - i\\sin(28\\theta)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"221\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>We plug these values into our equation and simplify to find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/3/3b353376a76d9d3783cc68f7d897232e29c7096c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(28\\theta)=\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"105\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/a/2ea845ed64af906198b329175d1037a58f357ce8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$28\\theta=\\pm 60 (mod 360)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"161\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>We now do casework.\n</p><p>Case <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/1/2d1befbd11149e2f39d6b134d0b82c6c55a3ed34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$28\\theta=60 (mod 360)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"147\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/f/6aff289ada55f7274889a51d92cb2e51ff0ed3e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7\\theta=15 (mod 90)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"129\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>We now proceed with the modular inverse to isolate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/7/727593f33ff6f1987613f03cda686da37b86a106.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7x=1 (mod 90)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"121\" height=\"20\" /> we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/8/638f55cd5570facc2150ef8519bc5d4244f0232e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=13$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" /> works. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/3/3e3009f880311a78f5a1a33fb0cb21a11bfce50d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$91\\theta=195 (mod 90)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"147\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/f/73f336527d4f4ca43e40daca7bdacb34766d1bd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta=15 (mod 90)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"120\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Case <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />&#160;:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/8/408298b1706a2b9c309190b45a653e81d48713e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$28\\theta=-60 (mod 360)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"161\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/d/7fd85f28e1928f46f0639907428c9d448996f5cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$28\\theta=300 (mod 360)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"156\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/0/ba0defe0c8f68bac74eeaeb84bd83ec5075e849c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7\\theta=75 (mod 90)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"129\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/1/82177f75ec8835ed89b7a627b81be39024898de7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta=75 (mod 90)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"120\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>We have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/5/0a573b6ee5c14ad61a9825fc6dce2b5e7bf8e08e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta= 15,75 (mod 90)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"146\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>We now list the solutions to each of these conditions for angles less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/2/c62a47cbc153efdf4611d8660429ea879be3f192.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$360$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Condition <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/4/524de7e171fe1f2a1d43f4c7c3ba5a3a4b06a008.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta=(15,105,195,285)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"173\" height=\"20\" />, Condition <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/4/db4d54805d9d6d038debba59bb73edfc500a350e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta=(75,165,255,345)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"173\" height=\"20\" />. \n</p><p>These are the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/3/f93f5c51ea4b04b4992b003b39479f29018f6bda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2n$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> values that satisfy the problem. We order them in increasing order and add the values in the even places.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/b/3ab10e762642c9a4a04ac13fb241d5f1a1ee63d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$75+165+255+345=\\boxed{840}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"231\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~jamespudi\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_II\" title=\"2001 AIME II\">2001 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2001 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2001 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2001\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2001 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2001 AIME II Problems/Problem 15\">Problem 15</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2001 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2001 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2001 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2001 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2001 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2001 AIME II Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2001 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2001 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2001 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2001 AIME II Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2001 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2001 AIME II Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2001 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2001 AIME II Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017042416\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.056 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.074 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 647/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1810/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 132/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 22047/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.538      1 -total\n 60.78%    7.621      1 Template:AIME_box\n 37.50%    4.702      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:3130:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017042416 and revision id 292541. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}